 path:[["Sept – Oct 2026","Early rounds","Chevening, Rhodes, Commonwealth, Knight-Hennessy and GKS undergraduate have closed for 2027. Note them for 2028."],
  ["Nov – Dec 2026","Peak season","US undergraduate (Jan 1) and PhD (Dec 1–15), DAAD, Eiffel nominations, HKPFS, SINGA, ETH/EPFL, Yenching, NYU Law, AAUW."],
  ["Jan 2027","Europe opens wide","Erasmus Mundus, Gates and Clarendon, Swedish and Finnish universities (Jan 15), Stipendium Hungaricum, IsDB, LSE and Hong Kong entrance awards."],
  ["Feb – Mar 2027","Asia & government schemes","Türkiye Bursları (Feb 20), GKS graduate, CSC China, Netherlands, Ireland GOI-IES, Master Mind, Pan African University, Manaaki NZ."],
  ["Apr – Jun 2027","Results & second chances","Offers arrive. MEXT embassy round (for 2028), Australia coursework awards, Saudi universities, Italian scholarships, Mexican and Brazilian calls."],
  ["Jun – Aug 2027","Graduate & prepare","Graduation, transcripts, visas, Italian DSU grants (Jul–Sept). Start building your 2028 applications if needed."],
  ["Aug – Oct 2027","2028 round opens","Chevening, Rhodes, Commonwealth, Knight-Hennessy, GKS undergraduate and Australian research rounds for 2028."],
  ["Sept – Oct 2027","Start","Begin your degree. In year one, apply for top-up awards inside your university."]],
 tips:[["Start with the deadline","Sort by deadline and work backwards. Most scholarships need 6–10 weeks to collect letters, test scores and translations."],
  ["Mind the official GPA","If a scholarship publishes a minimum, check it with the official conversion. If it only lists a typical GPA, a strong file can still win."],
  ["Tailor every essay","Name the programme's courses, professors and labs. Explain what you'll do after, and why that matters for your country or community."],
  ["Choose referees who know you","A lecturer who supervised your project writes a better letter than a famous name. Ask 6 weeks ahead and send them your CV."],
  ["Take the English test early","IELTS 7.0 or TOEFL 100 covers almost everything. Ask your university for an English Medium of Instruction letter too."],
  ["Contact professors","For research master's and PhDs (China, Japan, Korea, Canada, the US, Singapore), a supervisor's interest often decides funding."],
  ["Apply widely","Aim for 10–20 applications across 3–5 countries: a few dream options, many realistic ones and a couple of safe ones."],
  ["Show impact, not just grades","Leadership, volunteering, competitions, publications and work experience separate equal GPAs."],
  ["Never pay to apply","Government scholarships like CSC, MEXT, GKS, Türkiye Bursları, DAAD and Erasmus Mundus are free. Avoid agents who promise guaranteed awards."]]
